    "if_state": "The actual IF/IF_NOT macro executes iteration 0 before iteration 2. BindIf/BindIfNot always initialize else_block and end_block before branching or binding. The final iteration reads those initialized pointers. ELSE may null else_block deliberately; that state is checked. Nested macros have their own scoped state.",
    "hash_output": "Find assigns the output hash whenever it returns an empty insertion slot. Existing-entry hits need not assign it, and AddOrFind reads the output only after confirming that the returned entry is empty. The graph optimizer is single-threaded, with no intervening mutation between return and this check."
  },
